    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d478">

                <pb facs="0949" n="919" sameAs="frus:frus1958-60v02/pg919"/>

                <head>478. Telegram From the Mission at the United Nations to the Department of
                        State<anchor n="1" xml:id="d478-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic">New
                                York</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1959-12-11T00:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 11,
                                1959—midnight</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Delga 689. Re: Outer Space. Kuznetsov called on Lodge this morning. After certain
                    amount of preliminary bantering about possible shifts in US position and after
                    Lodge pressed Kuznetsov to accept Lebanon, latter expressed agreement on Lebanon
                    as 5th neutral. Regarding amendment on conference participation, which Lodge
                    repeated we must have, Kuznetsov said that he would speak against it and vote
                    against it but if amendment adopted, USSR would nevertheless vote for res and
                    participate in comite. Russians produced typewritten text, including names of
                    countries which we checked together.</p>
                <p>Lodge expressed his pleasure at results of negotiations which he hoped augured
                    well for future cooperation between US in outer space field as well as in other
                    areas.</p>
                <pb facs="0950" n="920" xml:id="pg920"/>
                <p>Lodge then reviewed cosponsorship to which we had previously agreed and suggested
                    addition of Japan. Kuznetsov agreed and proposed Romania also be added. Lodge
                    agreed. We told Kuznetsov we would wish to inform our group of results of our
                    discussions and would then be prepared to submit res early in afternoon. (This
                    mtg reported Delga 690.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d478-f2"/>)</p>
                <p>Res submitted to Secretariat immediately after lunch.<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d478-f3"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Lodge</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
